#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:0
msgid ""
"Check the system requirements for hardware-backed disk encryption on Ubuntu "
"Desktop, including the TPM, UEFI firmware and automatic unlocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:7
msgid "Topics: Installation Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:11
msgid "Hardware-backed disk encryption requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:13
msgid ""
"Ubuntu checks certain system requirements before it allows you to enable "
"{ref}`hardware-backed disk encryption <hardware-backed-disk-encryption>` "
"(TPM/FDE) on your system. Generally, **most systems based on Intel and AMD "
"processors made since 2018** are compatible with TPM/FDE. On most systems "
"made since 2021, the disk can unlock automatically by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:15
msgid "Your hardware must meet the following requirements to support TPM/FDE:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:17
msgid ""
"Your device comes with the Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) "
"version 2.5 or later with the following features:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:19
msgid ""
"It meets the Platform Configuration Register (PCR) usage and log "
"requirements of the Trusted Computing Group (TCG) EFI PC Client Platform "
"Profile specification (2.0 family)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:20
msgid ""
"It implements the TCG EFI Protocol spec (2.0 family). Some older UEFI "
"implementations only support 1.2 family versions of the TCG specifications, "
"which is insufficient for TPM/FDE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:22
msgid ""
"Your device has a PC-client Trusted Platform Module version 2 (TPM2) chip, "
"version 1.32 of the reference library specification or later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:24
msgid "Secure Boot is enabled and in Deployed Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:26
msgid "Automatic unlocking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:28
msgid ""
"Your disk can unlock automatically without a PIN or passphrase if the UEFI "
"firmware is verified or measured by a **hardware root of trust**. This is "
"generally the case for PCs made since 2021. Automatic unlocking is also "
"known as *TPM-only unlock*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:30
msgid ""
"To verify or measure the firmware, your device must feature a dedicated "
"security chip:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:32
msgid "The Boot Guard Authenticated Code Module (ACM) on Intel systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:33
msgid "Platform Secure Boot (PSB) enabled on AMD systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:36
msgid ""
"Certain hardware vendors might enable firmware options that alter your "
"system's chain of trust, such as the [Absolute Persistence](https://"
"www.absolute.com/platform/persistence) technology."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:38
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu installer alerts you to this. You can choose to disable the "
"feature if you have the permissions or you can ignore the notice to keep the "
"feature enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:41
msgid ""
"With a hardware root of trust, your hardware verifies the UEFI firmware "
"before the firmware runs, based on a read-only piece of code in your CPU. "
"This protects your disk encryption against threats such as malware that "
"targets your firmware, or supply-chain attacks while your hardware is "
"handled after manufacture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:43
msgid ""
"If your system does not have a hardware root of trust, the Ubuntu installer "
"makes it mandatory to add a PIN or passphrase. After installation, you can "
"disable the PIN or passphrase. However, your system won't be protected "
"against the described hardware and firmware threats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:46
msgid "Report bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/hardware-backed-disk-encryption-requirements.md:48
msgid ""
"If you think that your system should be eligible for TPM/FDE given these "
"requirements, but Ubuntu still doesn't enable TPM/FDE, [open a bug](https://"
"github.com/canonical/secboot/issues/new)."
msgstr ""
